{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-32-1","title":"Jeremiah 32:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jeremiah, being imprisoned by Zedekiah for his prophecy, 6 buys Hanameel's field. 13 Baruch must preserve the evidences, as tokens of the people's return. 16 Jeremiah in his prayer complains to God. 26 God confirms the captivity for their sins; 36 and promises a gracious return.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3415. B.C. 589. in the. 39:1,2; 52:4,5; 2Ki 25:1,2; 2Ch 36:11 the eighteenth. 25:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-2","title":"Jeremiah 32:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>then.The siege had commenced on the tenth month of the preceding year, and continued a year after, ending in the fifth month of the following year; consequently the siege must have lasted eighteen months and twenty-seven days. See 2 Ki 25:18.</p>\n<p>Jeremiah. 3,8; 33:1; 36:5; 37:21; 38:6; 39:13-15; Mt 5:12 in the. Ne 3:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-3","title":"Jeremiah 32:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Zedekiah. 2:30; 5:3; 2Ki 6:31,32; 2Ch 28:22 Wherefore. 26:8,9; 38:4; Ex 5:4; Am 7:13; Lu 20:2; Ac 6:12-14 Behold. 28,29; 21:4-7; 27:8; 34:2,3; 37:6-10; 38:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-4","title":"Jeremiah 32:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>37:17; 38:18,23; 39:4-7; 52:8-11; 2Ki 25:4-7; Eze 12:12,13 Eze 17:13-21; 21:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-5","title":"Jeremiah 32:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>until. 27:22; 34:4,5 though. 2:37; 21:4,5; 33:5; 37:10; Nu 14:41; 2Ch 13:12; 24:20; Pr 21:30 Eze 17:9,10,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-7","title":"Jeremiah 32:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Behold. 1Ki 14:5; Mr 11:2-6; 14:13-16 Anathoth. 1:1; 11:21; Jos 21:18,19 for. Le 25:23,34,49; Nu 35:2; Ru 4:4-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-8","title":"Jeremiah 32:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>court. 2; 33:1 Anathoth. 7; 1Ki 2:26; 1Ch 6:60 Then I. 1Sa 9:16,17; 10:3-7; 1Ki 22:25; Zec 11:11; Joh 4:53; Ac 10:17-28 that this.That it was by His appointment that I was to make this purchase; the whole of which was designed as a symbolical act, to shew the people, that although Judah and Jerusalem should be desolated, and the inhabitants carried captive to Babylon, yet there should be a restoration, when lands and possessions should be again enjoyed by their legal owners, in the same manner as formerly. During the famine that prevailed in the city, Hanameel probably wanted money to purchase bread, and his field would not be thought of much value in such circumstances, which may account for the stipulated sum being so very small; for at 2s. 6d. the shekel, it would only amount to about 2�. 2s. 6d.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-9","title":"Jeremiah 32:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>weighed. Ge 23:15,16; 1Ki 20:39; Es 3:9; Isa 55:2; *margins seventeen shekels of silver. or, seven shekels, and tenpieces of silver. Ge 37:28; Ho 3:2; Zec 11:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-10","title":"Jeremiah 32:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>I. 12,44; Isa 44:5 subscribed the evidence. Heb. wrote in the book. Jos 18:9; Isa 30:8 and sealed. De 32:34; Job 14:17; So 8:6; Da 8:26; Joh 3:33; 6:27; 2Co 1:22 Eph 1:13; 4:30; Re 7:2; 9:4 and took. 12,25,44; Ru 4:9-11; Isa 8:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-11","title":"Jeremiah 32:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>according. Lu 2:27; Ac 26:3; 1Co 11:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-12","title":"Jeremiah 32:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Baruch. 16; 36:4,5,16-19,26; 43:3-6; 45:1-5 Neriah. 51:59 and in. 2Co 8:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-14","title":"Jeremiah 32:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Take. 10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-15","title":"Jeremiah 32:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Houses. 37,43,44; 30:18; 31:5,12,24; 33:12,13; Am 9:14,15; Zec 3:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-16","title":"Jeremiah 32:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>I Prayed. 12:1; Ge 32:9-12; 2Sa 7:18-25; Eze 36:35-37; Php 4:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-17","title":"Jeremiah 32:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Ah. 1:6; 4:10; 14:13; Eze 9:8; 11:13 thou. 10:11,12; 27:5; 51:15,19; Ge 1:1-31; Ex 20:11; 2Ki 19:15; Ne 9:6 Ps 102:25; 136:5-9; 146:5,6; Isa 40:26-28; 42:5; 44:24; 45:12 Isa 48:12,13; Zec 12:1; Joh 1:1-3; Ac 7:49,50; 14:15; 17:24 Col 1:15,16; Heb 1:2,3,10-12; Re 4:11 there. 27; Ge 18:14; Job 42:2; Lu 1:37; 18:27 to hard for thee. or, hid from thee. Isa 46:9,10; Da 2:22; Ac 15:18; Eph 3:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-18","title":"Jeremiah 32:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>shewest. Ex 20:5,6; 34:7; Nu 14:18; De 5:9,10; 7:9,10 recompensest. Jos 7:24-26; 2Sa 21:1-9; 1Ki 14:9,10; 16:1-3; 21:21-24; 2Ki 9:26 Mt 23:32-36; 27:25 the Great. Ge 49:24; De 7:21; 10:17; Ne 1:5; Ps 50:1; 145:3-6; Isa 9:6; 10:21 Isa 57:15; Hab 1:12 the Lord. 10:16; 31:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-19","title":"Jeremiah 32:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Great. Isa 9:6; 28:29; 40:13; 46:10,11; Ro 11:33,34; Eph 1:11 work. Heb. doing. Ex 15:11; Da 4:35 for. 16:17; 23:24; 2Ch 16:9; Job 34:21; Ps 33:13-15; 34:15; Pr 5:21 Heb 4:13 to give. 17:10; 1Ki 8:32; Ps 62:12; Ec 12:14; Mt 16:27; Joh 5:29 Ro 2:6-10; 2Co 5:10; Re 2:23; 22:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-20","title":"Jeremiah 32:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>hast set. Ex 7:3; 10:2; De 4:34; 6:22; 7:19; Ne 9:10; Ps 78:43-51; 105:27-36 Ps 135:9; Ac 7:36 and hast. Ex 9:16; 2Sa 7:23; 1Ch 17:21; Ne 9:10; Isa 63:12; Da 9:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-21","title":"Jeremiah 32:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>brought. Ex 6:6; 13:14; Ps 105:37,43; 106:8-11 with a strong. Ex 6:1; 13:9; De 26:8; 1Ki 8:42; Ps 89:8-10; 136:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-22","title":"Jeremiah 32:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>which. Ge 13:15; 15:18-21; 17:7,8; 24:7; 28:13-15; 35:11,12; 50:24; Ex 13:5 Nu 14:16,30; De 1:8,35; 6:10,18,23; 7:13; 8:1; Jos 1:6; 21:43 Ne 9:15; Ps 105:9-11 a land. 11:5; Ex 3:8,17; 13:5; 33:1-3; De 26:9-11; Eze 20:6,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-23","title":"Jeremiah 32:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>possessed. Ne 9:15,22-25; Ps 44:2,3; 78:54,55; 105:44,45 but. 7:23,24; 11:7,8; Jud 2:11-13; 10:6-18; Ezr 9:7; Ne 9:26-30 Eze 20:8,18,21; Da 9:4-6,10-14; Zec 1:2-4 they have. Lu 17:10; Joh 15:14; Ga 3:10; Jas 2:10 therefore. Le 26:14-46; De 28:15-68; Jos 23:16; Ezr 9:7; La 1:8,18; 5:16,17 Da 9:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-24","title":"Jeremiah 32:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>mounts. or, engines of shot. 33:4; Eze 21:22 The mounts were huge terraces raised up to plant their engines on; and so formed as to be capable of being moved forwards towards the city. See Note on 2 Sa 20:15.</p>\n<p>the city is. 3,25,36; 21:4-7; 37:6-10 because. 14:12-15; 15:1-3; 16:4; 24:10; 52:6; La 2:21,22; 4:3-10; Eze 14:21 what. De 4:26; 31:16,17; 32:24,25; Jos 23:15,16; Zec 1:6; Mt 24:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-25","title":"Jeremiah 32:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>thou. 8-15 for. or, though. 24; Ps 77:19; 97:2; Joh 13:7; Ro 11:33,34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-27","title":"Jeremiah 32:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>God. Nu 16:22; 27:16; Ps 65:2; Isa 64:8; Lu 3:6; Joh 17:2; Ro 3:29,30 is. 17; Mt 19:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-28","title":"Jeremiah 32:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Behold. 3,24,36; 19:7-12; 20:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-29","title":"Jeremiah 32:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>and set. 17:27; 21:10; 27:8-10; 37:7-10; 39:8; 52:13; 2Ki 25:9; 2Ch 36:19 Isa 64:10,11; La 4:11; Mt 22:7 upon. 7:18; 19:13; 44:17-19,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-30","title":"Jeremiah 32:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>children. 2:7; 3:25; 7:22-26; De 9:7-12,22-24; 2Ki 17:9-20; Ne 9:16-37 Ps 106:6,7; Isa 63:10; Eze 16:15-22; 20:8,28; 23:43,44; Ac 7:51-53 from. 22:21; Ge 8:21; Eze 23:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-31","title":"Jeremiah 32:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>this city. 5:9-11; 6:6,7; 23:14,15; 1Ki 11:7,8; 2Ki 21:4-7,16; 22:16,17 2Ki 23:15; Eze 22:2-22; Mt 23:37; Lu 13:33,34 a provocation of mine anger. Heb. for my anger. that I. 27:10; 2Ki 23:27; 24:3,4; La 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-32","title":"Jeremiah 32:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>they. 2:26; Ezr 9:7; Ne 9:32-34; Isa 1:4-6,23; 9:14,15; Eze 22:6,25-29 Da 9:6,8; Mic 3:1-5,9-12; Zep 3:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-33","title":"Jeremiah 32:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>turned. 2:27; 7:24; 18:17; Eze 8:16; Ho 11:2; Zec 7:11 back. Heb. neck. rising. 7:13; 25:3,4; 26:5; 35:15; 44:4; 2Ch 36:15,16; Joh 8:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-34","title":"Jeremiah 32:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>7:30; 23:11; 2Ki 21:4-7; 23:6; 2Ch 33:4-7,15; Eze 8:5-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-35","title":"Jeremiah 32:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>they built. 7:31; 19:5,6; 2Ki 23:10; 2Ch 28:2,3; 33:6; Ps 106:37,38; Isa 57:5 Eze 16:20,21; 23:37 which. 7:31; Le 18:21; 20:2-5; De 18:10; 1Ki 11:33 to cause. Ex 32:21; De 24:4; 1Ki 14:16; 15:26,30; 16:19; 21:22; 2Ki 3:3; 21:11 2Ki 23:15; 2Ch 33:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-36","title":"Jeremiah 32:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>now. 16:12-15; Isa 43:24,25; 57:17,18; Eze 36:31,32; Ho 2:14; Ro 5:20 Eph 2:3-5 It. 3,24,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-37","title":"Jeremiah 32:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>I will gather.\"This promise,\" says Jerome, \"taken in its full extent was not made good to those that returned from captivity; because they were frequently infested with wars, as well by the kings of Syria and Egypt as by the rest of their neighbours; and they were finally subdued and destroyed by the Romans.\" God's word cannot fail; therefore there remaineth yet a rest for the ancient people of God.</p>\n<p>23:3,8; 29:14; 30:18; 31:10; 33:7; De 30:3-6; Ps 106:47 Isa 11:11-16; Eze 11:17; 34:12-14; 36:24; 37:21-25; 39:25-29 Ho 1:11; 3:5; Am 9:14,15; Ob 1:17-21; Zep 3:20 I will cause. 23:6; 33:16; Eze 34:25-28; Joe 3:20; Zec 2:4,5; 3:10; 14:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-38","title":"Jeremiah 32:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>24:7; 30:22; 31:1,33; Ge 17:7; De 26:17-19; Ps 144:15; Eze 11:19,20 Eze 36:28; 37:27; 39:22,28; Zec 13:9; Heb 8:10; 11:16; Re 21:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-39","title":"Jeremiah 32:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>I. 2Ch 30:12; Isa 52:8; Eze 11:19,20; 36:26; 37:22; Joh 17:21; Ac 4:32 2Co 13:11; Php 2:1,2 one way. 6:16; Isa 35:8; Joh 14:6; Heb 10:20 they may. 40; Ge 22:12; Ps 112:1; Pr 14:26,27; 23:17; Ac 9:31 for every. Heb. all days. for the. Ge 17:7; 18:19; De 5:29; 11:18-21; Ps 115:13-15; 128:6; Eze 37:25 Ac 2:39; 3:26; 13:33; Ro 11:16; 1Co 7:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-40","title":"Jeremiah 32:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>I will make. 31:31-33; 50:5; Ge 17:7-13; 2Sa 23:4; Isa 24:5; 55:3; 61:8 Lu 1:72-75; Ga 3:14-17; Heb 6:13-18; 7:24; 13:20 that I. Eze 39:29; Joh 10:27-30; Ro 8:28-39 from them. Heb. from after them. but I. 31:33; Eze 36:26; Heb 4:1; Jas 1:17; 1Pe 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-41","title":"Jeremiah 32:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>Yea, I. De 30:9; Isa 62:5; 65:19; Zep 3:17 and I. 18:9; 24:6; 31:28; Am 9:15 assuredly. Heb. in truth, or stability. Ho 2:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-42","title":"Jeremiah 32:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>Like. 31:28; Jos 23:14,15; Zec 8:14,15; Mt 24:35 so. 33:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-43","title":"Jeremiah 32:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>36; Eze 37:11-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-32-44","title":"Jeremiah 32:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>buy. 6-15 in the land. 17:26 for I. 37; 33:7,11,26; Ps 126:1-4 As an earnest of these promises, houses and lands shall again take a good price in Judah and Jerusalem; and though they now are almost valueless, there shall again be a sufficiency of purchasers. Trade shall revive, for they shall have money enough to buy land with; husbandry shall revive, for those that have money, shall covet to lay it out upon lands; laws shall again have their due course, for they shall subscribe evidences, and seal them.</p>"}]}